@@ -41,7 +41,11 @@ Retries of a run share the original deadline; cancelled/expired attempts cannot
 be relaunched under that run ID. Deadline zero retains existing unlimited-run
 semantics, while root-exit cleanup is always bounded.
 Startup acknowledgement has a separate 30-second bound even with deadline zero.
+Command resolution itself settles on cancellation or the earlier of the original
+deadline and the 30-second startup limit; a late target is cleaned without spawn.
 The helper uses a monotonic deadline after receiving the owner's remaining budget.
+After a Windows owner is lost across a service restart, orphan reconciliation
+records cleanup uncertainty without probing/killing a saved PID or retrying work.
 
 ## Adoption owned by Hermes
 
